# Sandbox-pinned root Cargo.lock for cargo 1.75 (rebuild recipe below)
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# The sandbox toolchain is cargo 1.75, which cannot parse manifests that use
# `edition = "2024"` (requires cargo >= 1.85). Two transitive deps of
# `redis 0.27` (pulled by the engine) hit that wall:
#   - url -> idna -> idna_adapter 1.2.2  (edition2024)
#   - tokio-retry 0.3 -> rand 0.10 -> getrandom 0.4 -> chacha20 -> cpufeatures 0.3 (edition2024)
# `cargo update` alone cannot fix it: every downgrade path is blocked by a
# semver requirement, and chacha20 >= 0.10 always resolves cpufeatures 0.3.x,
# which is also edition2024.
#
# THIS FILE
# A hand-pruned copy of the fresh lock: the chacha20, tokio-retry, cpufeatures,
# rand 0.10.3, rand_core 0.10.1 and getrandom 0.4.3 blocks are removed, the
# ` "tokio-retry",` line is dropped from redis's dep list, and the following
# are pinned to their last non-edition2024 versions:
#   idna_adapter 1.2.2 -> 1.1.0, url 2.5.8 -> 2.5.4, ahash 0.8.12 -> 0.8.11,
#   zerocopy 0.8.60 -> 0.8.48, tokio 1.53.2 -> 1.47.1
# With these removed the edition2024 parse errors disappear for `cargo test`.
#
# KNOWN CAVEAT
# `cargo test` in the sandbox compiles the engine against redis 0.27, whose
# `connection-manager` feature uses tokio-retry at runtime (it is not exercised
# by any test here — the engine tests do not touch the Redis connection manager).
# The Docker build uses its own lock + modern toolchain and is unaffected.
#
# REBUILD (when engine/Cargo.toml changes):
#   rm -f Cargo.lock && cargo update
#   cargo update -p idna_adapter@1.2.2 --precise 1.1.0
#   cargo update -p url@2.5.8 --precise 2.5.4
#   cargo update -p ahash@0.8.12 --precise 0.8.11
#   cargo update -p zerocopy@0.8.60 --precise 0.8.48
#   cargo update -p tokio@1.53.2 --precise 1.47.1
#   python3 scripts/prune_lock.py   # removes the edition2024 blocks
#
# This file is git-ignored (/Cargo.lock in .gitignore) and is local-only.
# It is NOT used by the Docker image.
